Paytm PML — Next-Round Take-Home
Wallet / P2P Transfer Service (Deploy & Reason)
Congratulations on clearing the earlier rounds. This next step is a bigger, hands-on exercise:
build it, deploy it, and reason about it. The surface is deliberately small — a wallet that lets
people hold a balance and transfer to each other — but money movement under concurrency
and retries is unforgiving, and that’s exactly what we want to see: the simplest correct design,
your reasoning about the trade-offs, and whether you can deploy and operate what you build.
Budget about a day of focused work (up to ~1.5 if you want to go deep). Everything runs on free
tiers — please spend ₹0. Use AI tools if you like; just tell us in the write-up what you directed vs.
decided.
What to build — a wallet / peer-to-peer transfer service
Users hold a balance (integer paise) and transfer to each other. You must never lose or create
money, never double-apply a retried transfer, and never let one user move another user’s
money.
Core API (keep it small):
1. Auth — users authenticate with a signed token (JWT or similar). The caller’s identity comes
from the verified token — never a trusted header or body field.
2. POST /accounts → get-or-create the caller’s wallet → { balance }. Idempotent: calling
twice returns the same wallet, never two.
